{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>As I live</b> — an expression of oath. <b>And the glory of YHWH shall fill all the earth</b>, <b>if they see the land</b> — this is an inverted verse: \"As I live, says YHWH, if all these men see the land, and My glory shall fill the earth\" — that My name not be profaned in this plague, so that they not say: \"Because YHWH was unable to bring them\" — that I not kill them suddenly all at once, but rather over a delay of forty years little by little. This is the language of Rashi. And it is not correct at all. Rather, these verses omit the oath-formula for the glory of the Higher One: \"As I live, and My glory shall fill all the earth, if all the men who test Me see the land\" — the matter is not so! And likewise, \"As I live, says YHWH, etc. if you come to the land\" (below, verses 28, 30) — the oath-formula is omitted. And thus even a commoner would abbreviate his oath: \"Thus may Elohim do to me and thus may He add\" (II Samuel 3:35) — they would not wish to articulate the curse. \"Thus may Elohim do to the enemies of David and thus may He add\" — they omit the blessing. And likewise we find that Caleb said to Joshua: \"You know the matter that YHWH spoke concerning me and concerning you\" (Joshua 14:6), and it is written: \"And Moses swore on that day, saying, Surely the land on which your foot has trodden shall be yours for an inheritance and for your children forever, because you fully followed after YHWH your Elohim\" (ibid. v. 9). And this is from what is stated here: \"But My servant Caleb, because a different spirit was with him and he fully followed after Me, I will bring him into the land to which he came, and his seed shall possess it\" (Numbers 14:24). And he mentions an oath in this promise, for all is bound to the verse \"But as I live,\" which is an oath as I have explained. And it says \"And Moses swore\" because Moses mentioned the oath. And by way of truth, \"But as I live and the glory of YHWH shall fill all the earth\" — a promise to Moses concerning forgiveness: He says that His glory shall fill all the earth through their seed and not through them."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:35.314710927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}